+## Probe-methodology lessons for any D3 sentinel (avoid false alarms)
+Two probe-contract pitfalls produced false FAILs on the first pass of this run (01:07:19Z) and were corrected before the final 10/10 (01:11:02Z). A scheduled sentinel MUST encode both or it will cry wolf:
+1. **CSP ships Report-Only in phase 1** (#1728 AC3): the header name is `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`; the enforced `Content-Security-Policy` flip is a future one-line rename. Lookup must accept both names — and header lookups must be case-insensitive (HTTP headers are; a plain case-sensitive dict is not).
+2. **CORS preflight needs preflight-shaped requests**: a bare `OPTIONS /` (no `Origin` + `Access-Control-Request-Method`) passes through to routing and returns 405 — that is the contract, not drift. A request from a NON-allowlisted origin returns 400 (`allow_credentials=true`, no wildcard — fail-closed, correct). Test with an allowlisted origin (`supremeai-studio.pages.dev`) and expect 200 + echoed ACAO; treat 400-from-foreign-origin as PASS.
